# NMU ThinkTank (ERTH MATCHING Platform) — Comprehensive System Analysis

## 1. Executive Summary & Core Purpose

**NMU ThinkTank** is a smart, skill-based team formation and project matching platform designed for New Mansoura University (NMU). It enables students, faculty, and research leads to post projects (general, research, or graduation) and intelligently match with team members based on technical skills, work style, schedule availability, and academic affinity.

### Key Capabilities:
- **Smart Skill Matching Engine**: Server-side multi-factor scoring algorithm (skills, complementarity, work style, schedule, reputation).
- **AI-Powered Assistance**: Groq AI (`llama-3.1-8b-instant`) integration for project description refinement and automatic skill extraction.
- **Project Workspaces**: Integrated Kanban task boards (`project_tasks`) and team chat (`project_messages`).
- **Academic Analytics**: Skill heatmap visualizer across university colleges and majors (`admin/heatmap.php`).
- **Peer Reputation System**: Multi-criterion peer evaluations (commitment, quality, collaboration).
- **Security & Reliability**: OTP email verification, session-based rate limiting, CSRF protection, and role-based access control (RBAC).

